<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
Health-check LaunchDaemon — runs deploy/health_check.sh every 5 minutes.

The audit found the old health check was log-only AND was never actually wired
into cron (setup_cron.sh installs bot jobs, not the health check). This daemon
makes the check REAL and self-supervising: StartInterval fires it every 300s and
it alerts to Telegram on failure (local API / tunnel / disk / restart-loop).

Install (or run deploy/install_supervision.sh):
    sudo cp deploy/launchd/com.wheellsverse.healthcheck.plist /Library/LaunchDaemons/
    sudo chown root:wheel /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.wheellsverse.healthcheck.plist
    sudo launchctl bootstrap system /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.wheellsverse.healthcheck.plist

TIP: also add an EXTERNAL uptime monitor (e.g. UptimeRobot on the public URL) —
a check that runs on this same Mac mini can't tell you when the whole box is down.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.wheellsverse.healthcheck</string>

    <key>UserName</key>
    <string>jhonwheeler</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/Users/jhonwheeler/wheellsverse_bots/deploy/health_check.sh</string>
    </array>

    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>300</integer>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/jhonwheeler/Library/Logs/wheellsverse/healthcheck.stdout.log</string>

    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/jhonwheeler/Library/Logs/wheellsverse/healthcheck.stderr.log</string>

    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>
</dict>
</plist>
